          "ruleId": "crux/advertised-one-liner-is-404-and-the-pipeline-cannot-fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Commit d1d510bba replaced the 404ing https://paiml.com/apr/install.sh with https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paiml/aprender/main/scripts/install.sh. Measured now: that URL is ALSO 404, because scripts/install.sh is not on main until this PR merges; the branch path (.../PMAT-3365-apr-install-script/scripts/install.sh) returns 200. The 404 resolves on merge. What does NOT resolve is the shape of the advertised command: `curl -LsSf <404> | sh` returns curl_rc=22, sh_rc=0 and PIPELINE rc 0. curl -sS still prints 'curl: (22) ...' to stderr, so an interactive user sees something; a Dockerfile RUN, a CI step, a provisioning script or any `set -e` caller sees success and continues with no apr installed."
          },
