              "raw/main (pre-merge)": 404,
              "raw/PMAT-3365-apr-install-script": 200
            },
            "failure_scenario": "A Dockerfile line `RUN curl -LsSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paiml/aprender/main/scripts/install.sh | sh` succeeds and the image ships with no apr; the failure surfaces at the next layer as 'apr: not found' with no trace of the install step having failed. The same holds for any transient network error or a future rename of the file on main, and no row of install_test.sh fetches the advertised URL at all, so nothing in this PR can detect it."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "crux/gate-never-runs-on-a-release",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "install-script.yml's `on:` keys are exactly ['pull_request', 'push'] - no `release:`, no `schedule:`, no `workflow_dispatch:`. The header argues, correctly, that a parity gate must run when either side of the coupling moves, and it lists binary-release.yml and nightly.yml in the paths filter. But the thing install.sh is actually coupled to is the ASSET a release produced, and the workflow can only fire on a file edit. A release cut from an older tag (binary-release.yml runs the workflow file AT THE TAG), a change to the release matrix made anywhere outside those two files, or a publish that simply fails to attach the aarch64 asset, all change the asset set with no push to a watched path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/install-script.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 18
                }
