              "-c",
              "<mutant M2: expected=$(awk ...) -> expected=$(sha256_of \"$tmp_dir/archive.tar.gz\"); then row 14's grep, the five network-free rows, and one real --version v0.67.0 install against the mutant>"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "85a64c005987054b06d4b401b9895fd9a1ffa5b57277634ddeed8436ec3918ef",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "mutant": "scripts/install.sh:245 expected=$(awk '{print $1}' \"$tmp_dir/archive.tar.gz.sha256\") -> expected=$(sha256_of \"$tmp_dir/archive.tar.gz\")",
            "killed": false,
            "failure_scenario": "The supply-chain check the installer advertises is silently disabled - by a refactor, a bad merge, or a tampered release whose .sha256 is served from the same compromised origin as the tarball - and the whole gate stays green, because the only row that names the checksum measures the script's own comment text. This is a test that can only fail if someone edits an error MESSAGE."
          }
