          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The 'Verifying install' step cannot change the installer's exit code. Line 263 is `installed_version=$(\"$INSTALL_DIR/apr\" --version 2>&1) || warn \"could not run ...\"` and line 264 is `[ -n \"${installed_version:-}\" ] && ok \"$installed_version\"`; neither arm can fail the script. Measured with a mutant that truncates the binary immediately after `mv` (the partial cross-filesystem copy $TMPDIR-on-another-fs makes possible): a ZERO-BYTE apr was installed, the installer printed 'Done' and exited 0, and it printed NO warning at all - an empty file with mode 755 is exec'd as an empty shell script, so `--version` returns rc 0 with empty output and even the `|| warn` arm does not fire. A second mutant deleting `chmod +x` (line 259) also survives every row, because the tar member already carries mode 755 - so the only line that would rescue a non-executable release asset is itself unexercised."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/install.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 262
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "<mutant M3: truncate the binary immediately after mv (: > \"$INSTALL_DIR/${BINARY_NAME}\"), simulating a partial cross-filesystem copy; then one real --version v0.67.0 install and read the installer's exit code>"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "1d475f01e8869011555688705ff33b5a25bfc5197c00e6aaec1b38c8648f796b",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "corroborating_commands": [
              [
                "bash",
                "-c",
                "<mutant M4: delete chmod +x \"$INSTALL_DIR/${BINARY_NAME}\"; then one real --version v0.67.0 install and stat -c %a on the result>"
              ]
            ],
            "mutants": [
              "scripts/install.sh:258 truncate after mv (KILLED, by row 7's `grep -qE '^apr [0-9]'` over empty output)",
              "scripts/install.sh:259 delete chmod +x (SURVIVED; installed mode is 755 either way)"
            ],
            "failure_scenario": "A cross-filesystem `mv` that is interrupted, a wrong-architecture or glibc-mismatched asset, or a cuda asset chosen by detect_variant() on a driver-only host with no CUDA userspace: in every case apr lands on PATH broken and install.sh exits 0 having printed 'Done'. The user's next command is `apr --help`, and the installer has already told them the install succeeded."
          }
        },
