          "ruleId": "install-test/self-test-classifier-does-not-discriminate",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "`--self-test` is the row the CI workflow runs FIRST, to prove the suite is not vacuous before trusting it. Its verdict is decided at line 92 by `if [ \"$mrc\" = 1 ]` - FAIL, else ok - so every exit code other than 1 is read as 'the guard removal changed the mutant's behaviour'. Truth table over {0,1,2,126,127}: four of the five print ok, including 2 (the file's own documented environment/vacuous code) and 126/127 (the mutant could not be executed at all). The other polarity is worse and is measured, not hypothesised: with the network stubbed out, the mutant's real nightly download fails, error() exits 1, and the self-test prints 'FAIL self-test mutant still rejected --nightly+--version - guard removal had no effect (test is vacuous)' and returns 1. A dead network is reported as a defect in the test's discriminating power."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/tests/install_test.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 92
                }
