          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "for mrc in 0 1 2 126 127; do <evaluate install_test.sh:92 `if [ \"$mrc\" = 1 ]`>; done; PATH=<stub-curl>:$PATH bash scripts/tests/install_test.sh --self-test"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "9b8d2c4d337678728aecd50e2950462f4e1394e8f41367ecf93ad8d82bec1522",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "Two symmetric failures from one classifier. (a) The mutation stops working - python3 missing, the mutant tree unwritable, sh unable to exec it - and the self-test reports ok, so the CI step that exists to prove the suite discriminates passes while proving nothing. (b) GitHub is briefly unreachable and the same step goes red with a message blaming the test suite's design, sending whoever triages it to read install_test.sh instead of the network. This repository's standing rule is that a guard running a subprocess must classify env-death separately from a code defect; this one classifies neither."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "install-test/green-over-five-of-fourteen-rows-when-github-is-unreachable",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "install_test.sh's own header states the convention: 'Exit codes follow this repo's scripts/tests/*_test.sh convention: 0 pass, 1 a row genuinely failed, 2 environment/vacuous (no network, no curl, script missing) - an environment that cannot run the gate must never report ok.' The network branch does not follow it. With curl stubbed to exit 6, the suite prints the ENV line and then 'install_test.sh: 5 row(s), all ok' and EXITS 0: `red` is still 0, and `exit \"$red\"` is the last line. Nine of fourteen rows - every row that downloads anything, i.e. the entire point of the gate - vanish into a green. The trigger is not exotic: network_check() and six of the rows each hit https://api.github.com/repos/paiml/aprender/releases/latest UNAUTHENTICATED, 7 calls per run (measured with a logging curl shim over one instrumented full run: 22 curl invocations, 7 of them to that endpoint, 155.6 MiB of release assets), against a documented limit of 60 per hour PER IP. This reviewer's box went from used 48 / remaining 12 to used 57 / remaining 3 on that single run. The self-hosted clean-room pool shares one egress IP across the fleet, so exhaustion is a scheduling accident, and its symptom is a green run that tested five argument-parsing rows."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/tests/install_test.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 176
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "st=$(mktemp -d); printf '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 6\\n' > \"$st/curl\"; chmod +x \"$st/curl\"; PATH=\"$st:$PATH\" bash scripts/tests/install_test.sh; printf 'exit_code=%s\\n' \"$?\""
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "31d2ced5ce857bc9a3461661b6e8ffd51afafc053b5ef473a42703ac56bf0214",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "corroborating_commands": [
              [
                "bash",
                "-c",
                "sort <curl-shim call log from one instrumented full run> | uniq -c; curl -fsSL https://api.github.com/rate_limit | jq -c .resources.core"
              ]
            ],
            "measured": {
              "exit_code_with_no_network": 0,
              "rows_run": 5,
              "rows_skipped": 9,
              "api_github_com_calls_per_run": 7,
              "bytes_downloaded_per_run": 163128602,
              "rate_limit_core": {
                "limit": 60,
                "before": {
                  "used": 48,
                  "remaining": 12
                },
                "after": {
                  "used": 57,
                  "remaining": 3
                }
              }
            },
            "failure_scenario": "binary-release.yml renames the stable asset. The next install-script.yml run happens while the shared runner IP is over its 60/hour unauthenticated budget (or GitHub has a five-minute blip): network_check fails, the suite exits 0, the check goes green, the PR merges, and the gate has certified a naming contract it never tested. The fix is small and the file already knows what it should be - `exit 2` on the ENV branch, and either an authenticated GITHUB_TOKEN header or a single cached tag lookup reused across rows."
          }
        }
